#!/bin/bash
# vencord-discord: puts the Vencord build in ~/repositories/Vencord into
# Discord stable, and restarts Discord. The macOS and Linux counterpart of
# ~/.local/bin/vencord-discord.ps1 on Windows.
#
#   vencord-discord inject       inject unless Discord already loads this build
#                                (080-vencord runs this after every build; on
#                                Linux, 020-flatpak-packages and the
#                                vencord-discord-inject.path user unit too)
#   vencord-discord restart      quit Discord and start it again
#   vencord-discord dev [args]   pnpm i, pnpm build [args], inject, restart:
#                                one round of plugin work, for a person or an
#                                agent. Renderer-only changes would also load
#                                with Cmd/Ctrl+R; a plugin's native.ts, the
#                                patcher and the preload need the restart.
#
# `pnpm inject` runs Vencord's installer against this build
# (VENCORD_DEV_INSTALL): it renames Discord's resources/app.asar to _app.asar
# and writes a stub app.asar that requires the build's dist/patcher.js.
# Nothing has to be closed for that; a running Discord picks Vencord up when it
# next starts.
#
# macOS: Discord.app from the discord cask. Discord replaces its whole bundle
# when it updates, which drops the stub until the next inject.
# Linux: the --user Flatpak from 01-fedora/020-flatpak-packages. Discord runs
# from the Flatpak's deployment, which every Flatpak update replaces. The
# installer resolves the active deployment and lets the sandbox read the build
# (flatpak --user override --filesystem).
set -e

VENCORD_DIR="$HOME/repositories/Vencord"
PLATFORM="$(uname -s)"
case "$PLATFORM" in
    Darwin)
        DISCORD_LOCATION="/Applications/Discord.app"
        RESOURCES="$DISCORD_LOCATION/Contents/Resources"
        ;;
    Linux)
        DISCORD_LOCATION="$HOME/.local/share/flatpak/app/com.discordapp.Discord"
        RESOURCES="$DISCORD_LOCATION/current/active/files/discord/resources"
        ;;
    *)
        echo "error: vencord-discord does not support $PLATFORM" >&2
        exit 1
        ;;
esac

injected() {
    [ -f "$RESOURCES/_app.asar" ] &&
        grep -qF 'repositories/Vencord/dist/patcher.js' "$RESOURCES/app.asar" 2>/dev/null
}

# Returns 0 when injected, 1 when it could not be, 2 when there is no Discord
# to inject into.
do_inject() {
    if [ ! -d "$RESOURCES" ]; then
        echo "notice: Discord is not installed at $DISCORD_LOCATION; not injecting Vencord" >&2
        return 2
    fi
    if injected; then
        echo "debug: Vencord is already injected into Discord" >&2
        return 0
    fi
    if [ ! -f "$VENCORD_DIR/dist/patcher.js" ]; then
        echo "error: $VENCORD_DIR has no build to inject; 080-vencord builds it" >&2
        return 1
    fi
    # runInstaller.mjs exits 0 even when the installer fails, so the result
    # is checked rather than the exit code.
    (cd "$VENCORD_DIR" && pnpm inject --location "$DISCORD_LOCATION") || true
    if injected; then
        echo "notice: injected Vencord into Discord" >&2
        return 0
    fi
    if [ "$PLATFORM" = Darwin ]; then
        echo "error: could not inject Vencord into Discord; if the installer could not write to Discord.app, give your terminal App Management (System Settings > Privacy & Security)" >&2
    else
        echo "error: could not inject Vencord into Discord; see the installer's output above" >&2
    fi
    return 1
}

discord_running() {
    if [ "$PLATFORM" = Darwin ]; then
        pgrep -x Discord >/dev/null
    else
        flatpak ps --columns=application 2>/dev/null | grep -qx com.discordapp.Discord
    fi
}

stop_discord() {
    discord_running || return 0
    if [ "$PLATFORM" = Darwin ]; then
        osascript -e 'quit app "Discord"' >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
    else
        flatpak kill com.discordapp.Discord 2>/dev/null || true
    fi
    i=0
    while discord_running && [ "$i" -lt 30 ]; do
        sleep 1
        i=$((i + 1))
    done
    if discord_running && [ "$PLATFORM" = Darwin ]; then
        pkill -x Discord || true
        sleep 2
    fi
}

start_discord() {
    if [ "$PLATFORM" = Darwin ]; then
        open "$DISCORD_LOCATION"
    else
        setsid -f flatpak run --user com.discordapp.Discord >/dev/null 2>&1
    fi
}

case "${1:-}" in
    inject)
        status=0
        do_inject || status=$?
        if [ "$status" -eq 1 ]; then
            exit 1
        fi
        ;;
    restart)
        stop_discord
        start_discord
        ;;
    dev)
        shift
        if ! (cd "$VENCORD_DIR" && pnpm i --config.confirmModulesPurge=false && pnpm build "$@"); then
            echo "error: building Vencord in $VENCORD_DIR failed" >&2
            exit 1
        fi
        status=0
        do_inject || status=$?
        if [ "$status" -eq 2 ]; then
            echo "error: no Discord to load the build into" >&2
        fi
        if [ "$status" -ne 0 ]; then
            exit 1
        fi
        stop_discord
        start_discord
        echo "notice: Discord restarted on the new build" >&2
        ;;
    *)
        echo "usage: vencord-discord inject | restart | dev [pnpm build arguments]" >&2
        exit 2
        ;;
esac
